    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0368" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg252"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1560.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Commissioner Smith to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <lb/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 29, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I send you herewith an English translation
                    of the election decree and electoral law, which has only just now been
                    completed. Furthermore, copies of the English translation will be mailed to you
                    when ready. I am having them printed for the convenience and instruction of the
                    observers and others who may require them.</p>
                <p>I am writing this letter in the first person, as you doubtless know that Mr.
                    White is still in the Cibao, where, judging from his movements so far and his
                    plans so far as known, he is likely to remain for a considerable time, unless
                    previously recalled by you.</p>
                <p>Respectfully [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Commission: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ch. Cogswell Smith</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d344-a1.xml" xpointer="d344-a1"/>
            </div>
